# Force LF line endings in the working tree for every text file, on every
# platform, regardless of core.autocrlf.
#
# Why this matters specifically for this project: forge-prep's tests pin
# exact byte counts, SHA-256 content hashes, and a golden JSON snapshot
# (tests/fixtures/golden_sample_corpus_audit.json) against the files in
# examples/sample-corpus/ and tests/fixtures/. Without this file, Windows
# runners check out with autocrlf=true and every LF becomes CRLF — one
# extra byte per line. That silently changes size_bytes, char_count,
# token_estimate, and every content hash the auditor computes, and fails
# the golden-snapshot test even though nothing about the tool's behavior
# actually changed. `text=auto` still lets Git auto-detect genuinely binary
# files (there are none of consequence in this repo today) and leave them
# alone; `eol=lf` is what actually forces the working-tree normalization.
* text=auto eol=lf
